# DTF tier manifest: npm-version-route-dist-tags (artifact-keeper#5063, PR #5113)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams.mock-npm-tags (an npm upstream on
# 172.16.<slot>.86; see fixtures/mock_npm_tags.py).
#
# THE BUG: GET /npm/{repo}/{package}/{version} and the scoped form answered 404
# for a dist-tag such as `latest`, while an exact version worked. The npm registry
# resolves a tag on this route, and clients and scripts use /{package}/latest to
# find the current version. format-conformance's npm plugin only reads dist-tags
# from the packument, so it never exercised this route with a tag.
#
#   (FIX) `latest` and a custom tag return the tagged version's document on Local
#         (latest derived, `next` stored), Remote and Virtual; `latest` on a scoped
#         package on Remote and Virtual.
#         On an age-gated Remote, and a Virtual over it, `latest` resolves to the
#         newest version old enough to download and `old` resolves.
#         RED on 1.11.10: each is 404.
#   (CONTROL) both images: an exact version resolves on every repository type, and
#         an unknown tag is 404. An exact version wins over a stored tag of the same
#         name. A tag naming an unlisted version is 404. On the age-gated Remote a
#         tag naming a gated version is 404, and the exact gated version is still
#         served on this route (the gate applies at download).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-npm-tags"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
